                <pb facs="0644" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/170.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Leishman to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-04-30"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 30, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Leishman says the reports from Hadjin and other points indicate that trouble
                    in disturbed Provinces has almost ceased, the change of Government and arrival
                    of troops having most salutary effect, and expressed opinion that good order
                    soon will be completly restored.</p>
            </div>
